      "writtenOn": "2023-07-11T08:06:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your comment. There are several key takeaways:\n\n1. In the latest `rand.h`, boringssl provides only three APIs:\n- `RAND_bytes`: for generating output using the PRNG\n- `RAND_get_system_entropy_for_custom_prng`: for getting output from the TRNG\n- `RAND_cleanup`\n\nI can call one of the first two APIs to get random output generated by the PRNG or TRNG, respectively.\n\n2. Currently, pvmfw provides entropy through `CRYPTO_sysrand`, but this will soon be deprecated. We should switch to one of the two options described in go/boringssl-entropy. When clients use boringssl, it will add the entropy internally as needed, so clients don\u0027t need to worry about it.\n\nIs this correct?",
