      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T11:13:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi David, thanks for chipping in and clearing all of this up for us!\n\nSo, to summarize, `vmbase` (which is an internal low-level library of pvmfw) should:\n\n- keep using the TRNG for `CRYPTO_sysrand{,_for_seed}` (soon-to-be `getentropy`; b/290898063), which BSSL uses to seed its internal PRNG;\n- keep exposing a direct API for the TRNG (currently exposed through `fill_with_entropy` and its syntactic sugar `random_array`) as this seems to be required by some `vmbase` clients, according to previous comments;\n- start exposing a `RAND_bytes` wrapper (say \"`fill_with_pseudo_random`\"/\"`pseudo_random_array`\") to allow its clients to get pseudo-random bytes where their use-cases don\u0027t require full TRNG (the original goal of b/280032923, which this CL addresses)\n\nand, in particular, this CL will address the last point.\n\nAm I missing anything?",
      "parentUuid": "b37f97e7_493fdb2c",
